# Game regression fixes

The user requests fixes for best scores, arrow navigation, reduced motion and unwanted sound, following docs/README.md and its requirements. The user requires a plan and a separate subagent for each fix; the root agent reviews and verifies without editing code.

Plan: delegate scoring, keyboard navigation, motion and silence in that order, then review and run the full checks. Only one subagent can run alongside the root. Each agent owns its implementation and focused regression checks; no package or specification changes are needed.

Initial inspection: rememberBest always overwrites; GameStatus falls back to 0; Board has no arrow handler; card/status CSS omit reduced-motion overrides; use-game contains synthesized match/win tones. The working tree was initially clean. Locked dependency installation is running. Root has read the loader and all project specification documents. Agents must load their own applicable context.

